# | msgid "Output buffer"
# | msgid "Output device"
#: ui/config/output_group.py:245 ui/config/playback.py:142
msgid "The device's"
msgstr "デバイスの既定"

#: ui/config/output_group.py:249
msgid ""
"<p>The rate this output's device runs at; the main output's sound is "
"converted to it (a band-limited interpolator, with the clocks' drift). "
"The device's: its own format (WASAPI's shared mix format), the lowest "
"latency. Another rate: in exclusive mode the device runs at it; shared, "
"the system converts it (WASAPI (cpal)'s usual stream, more latency).</p>"
msgstr ""
"<p>この出力のデバイスが動作するサンプルレート。メイン出力の音をこのレートに変換します（帯域制限補間、クロックのドリフト込み）。デバイスの既定:"
" デバイス自身のフォーマット（WASAPI 共有のミックスフォーマット）で、レイテンシーが最も小さくなります。ほかのレート: "
"排他モードではデバイスがそのレートで動作し、共有モードではシステムが変換します（WASAPI (cpal) "
"の通常のストリーム、レイテンシー増）。</p>"

# | msgid "" "<p>Audio queued in the output device ahead of what is heard,
# with
# | the " "time stretch off. Smaller answers sooner (play, pause, seek, CUE
# | calls, " "volume); too small drops out when the computer is busy.</p>"
# | msgid "" "<p>Audio queued in the output device ahead of what is heard.
# | Smaller " "answers sooner (play, pause, seek, CUE calls, volume, tempo);
# too
# | small " "drops out when the computer is busy. With the time stretch, a
# seek
# | plays " "the original for its first tens of ms (the same pitch, at its own
# "
# | "tempo).</p>"
# | small " "drops out when the computer is busy. With the time stretch on, a
# | seek is " "heard tens of ms later (the position playing goes on
# | meanwhile).</p>"
# | the " "time stretch on or off. Smaller answers sooner (play, pause, seek,
# | CUE " "calls, volume, tempo); too small drops out when the computer is
# | busy.</p>"
# | msgid "" "<p>The native engine's audio queued ahead of the output device,
# | with the " "time stretch on or off. Smaller answers sooner (play, pause,
# | seek, CUE " "calls, volume, tempo); too small drops out when the computer
# is
# | busy. The" " device's own latency comes after it (shown under the
# | meter).</p>"
# | msgid "" "<p>The native engine's audio queued ahead of the output device.
# | small " "drops out when the computer is busy. The device's own latency
# comes
# | after" " it (shown under the meter).</p>"
# | msgid "" "<p>The audio kept ahead of this output's device, from the main
# | output's " "mix. Smaller is heard sooner; too small drops out when the
# | computer is " "busy. Its device's own latency comes after it.</p>"
#: ui/config/output_group.py:258
msgid ""
"<p>The audio kept ahead of this output's device, from the main output's "
"mix: the least it holds whatever the two devices' periods (it holds up to"
" one main device period more as they fall). Smaller is heard sooner; too "
"small drops out when the computer is busy. Its device's own latency comes"
" after it.</p>"
msgstr ""
"<p>メイン出力のミックスからこの出力のデバイスの前にためておくオーディオ: 2 "
"つのデバイスの周期がどう重なっても少なくともこれだけは保ちます（重なり方によってメインデバイスの 1 "
"周期分多くなることがあります）。小さいほど早く聞こえ、小さすぎるとコンピューターが忙しいときに音が途切れます。デバイス自体のレイテンシーはその後に加わります。</p>"

#: ui/config/output_group.py:265
msgid ""
"<p>This device's clock against the main output's: how much faster (+) or "
"slower (-) it runs, in parts per million. The output is resampled by it "
"(a band-limited interpolator), so it neither runs dry nor fills up, and "
"nothing is repeated or dropped. A few tens to a few hundred ppm is usual "
"between two devices.</p>"
msgstr ""
"<p>メイン出力に対するこのデバイスのクロックの差: どれだけ速く（+）または遅く（-）動くかを "
"ppm（百万分率）で表します。出力はこの分だけリサンプルされるため（帯域制限補間）、バッファーが空になったりあふれたりせず、サンプルの繰り返しや欠落もありません。2"
" つのデバイスの間では数十〜数百 ppm が普通です。</p>"

#: ui/config/output_group.py:270
msgid "Mix the master in"
msgstr "マスターを混ぜる"

#: ui/config/output_group.py:272
msgid ""
"<p>The headphones carry the channels whose CUE is on (before their "
"faders) and, with this on, the master, mixed by the CUE / MASTER mix (a "
"controller's knob moves it). Off for a controller that mixes the master "
"into its headphones itself (the DDJ-400's CUE / MASTER knob, in analog): "
"the headphones output then carries the CUE alone, silent while no CUE is "
"on.</p>"
msgstr ""
"<p>ヘッドホンには CUE をオンにしたチャンネル（フェーダー前）が出力され、この項目をオンにするとマスターも CUE / MASTER "
"のバランスで混ざります（コントローラーのつまみで調整）。コントローラーがヘッドホンにマスターを自分で混ぜる場合（DDJ-400 の CUE / "
"MASTER つまみ: アナログ）はオフにしてください: ヘッドホン出力は CUE だけになり、CUE がすべてオフのときは無音です。</p>"

#: ui/config/output_group.py:280
msgid ""
"<p>The master's share in the headphones: 0 % the CUE alone, 100 % the "
"master alone. A controller's CUE / MASTER knob moves it as it is "
"turned.</p>"
msgstr ""
"<p>ヘッドホンでのマスターの割合: 0 % で CUE だけ、100 % でマスターだけ。コントローラーの CUE / MASTER "
"つまみを回すとそれに従います。</p>"

